IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales): the nouns shared by the modules.
--
-- Only declarations: no rules.
-- The test a noun passes to be here is that a witness of ordinary competence could state it
-- (is this an Act, a regulation, an instrument made under an Act?); what the Act then makes of it is a rule,
-- and lives in the module for the provision that says so.
--
-- The time module (nsw-interpretation-time.l4) stands alone and keeps its own nouns.

-- What a rule of this Act is applied to.
-- Section 3(1): "instrument" is an instrument made under an Act and includes one made under such an instrument;
-- Schedule 4 "statutory rule" is a regulation, by-law, rule or ordinance made or approved by the Governor, or a rule of court.
DECLARE TextKind IS ONE OF
    AnActText
    AStatutoryRuleText
    AnEnvironmentalPlanningInstrumentText
    AnotherInstrumentText

-- A House of Parliament (Schedule 4: Legislative Council, Legislative Assembly).
DECLARE Chamber IS ONE OF
    TheLegislativeCouncil
    TheLegislativeAssembly

-- The grammatical number of a word or expression (section 8).
DECLARE GrammaticalNumber IS ONE OF
    SingularForm
    PluralForm

-- The thing a function-like word names (section 3(2), 48).
DECLARE FunctionLike IS ONE OF
    APower
    AnAuthority
    ADuty
    AnotherKindOfFunction
